course: dictionary
lesson: 405
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Appetite» is one of these words. In «Appetite often drops during an infection», the clues are drops and infection, which are about being unwell and not wanting to eat. So appetite means the feeling of wanting to eat food.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «She has an appetite for adventure» is about wanting something very much, not about food. The words for adventure are the clue, so here appetite means a strong wish or liking for something. Ask yourself: is this sentence about eating, or about wanting something?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "a strong wish for" or "the feeling of wanting to eat" and see which one makes sense. If neither fits, read on, and then look the word up in a dictionary.
fact: Appetite is a noun: an appetite, two or more appetites.
fact: «Appetite» means the feeling of wanting to eat food.
fact: «Appetite» can also mean a strong wish or liking for something, as in «an appetite for adventure».
fact: Useful phrases include «a good appetite», «lose your appetite» and «work up an appetite».
fact: Exercise and fresh air can increase your appetite, while illness can make you lose it.
exercise: «Appetite often drops during an infection.» What does appetite mean here? | A strong wish for adventure | *The feeling of wanting to eat food | A bright light in the dark | A loud noise made by an animal
exercise: Mia says, «She has an appetite for adventure.» What does appetite mean in this sentence? | A type of school lunch | *A strong wish or liking for something | A kind of sleep | The feeling of wanting to eat food
exercise: Which phrase means you have stopped wanting to eat? | work up an appetite | an appetite for adventure | a good appetite | *lose your appetite
test: Exercise and fresh air can ___ your appetite. Which word fits best? | ignore | decrease | forget | *increase
test: Which sentence uses appetite to mean a strong wish or liking for something? | His appetite was small after the flu. | He had no appetite for his soup. | The appetite was served with rice. | *She has a huge appetite for learning new words.
exam: Read this: «Appetite often drops during an infection; eating little for a day or two is fine, but drinking enough is important.» What does the sentence suggest you should do when your appetite drops? | Stop drinking anything until you feel better | Eat as much as you can every hour | Skip all food and drink for a week | *Keep drinking enough, even if you eat little
